{
  "tema": 6066,
  "slug": "he-hecho-perfecto-hacer",
  "titulo": "Hacer in the present perfect",
  "subtitulo": "¿Ya has hecho la tarea?",
  "foto": "t02.jpg",
  "regla": "Hacer in the present perfect is haber in the present + the irregular participle hecho (never hacido). Hecho never changes: he hecho, has hecho, ha hecho, hemos hecho, han hecho.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Build it with **haber** in the present + **hecho**. The participle of **hacer** is irregular: **hecho**, never hacido."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "he / has / ha / hemos / han",
            "+",
            "hecho"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "Hacer"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "he hecho"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "has hecho"
            ],
            [
              "él, ella, usted",
              "ha hecho"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros, nosotras",
              "hemos hecho"
            ],
            [
              "ellos, ellas, ustedes",
              "han hecho"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Hecho** never changes for gender or number: **he hecho la tarea**, **han hecho cambios**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Nothing goes between **haber** and **hecho**. Pronouns go before: **ya lo he hecho**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Weather works too: **ha hecho calor**, **ha hecho frío** (_it has been hot, cold_)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Spelling: **hecho** has an **h**. **Echo** is from **echar** (_to throw_)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "In Mexico, **hice** is more common for a finished action. **He hecho** shines with **ya**, **todavía no**, **nunca**, **alguna vez**, **este año**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "¿Ya ==has hecho== la tarea?",
              "en": "Have you done your homework yet?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Esta semana ==ha hecho== mucho calor en Tijuana.",
              "en": "It has been very hot in Tijuana this week."
            },
            {
              "es": "Nunca ==he hecho== tortillas de harina desde cero.",
              "en": "I've never made flour tortillas from scratch."
            },
            {
              "es": "Mi hermana ==ha hecho== tamales para toda la familia.",
              "en": "My sister has made tamales for the whole family."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Qué ==han hecho== ustedes este fin de semana?",
              "en": "What have you all done this weekend?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Todavía no ==hemos hecho== la composta.",
              "en": "We haven't made the compost yet."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Alguna vez ==has hecho== jiu-jitsu?",
              "en": "Have you ever done jiu-jitsu?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Este año los vecinos ==han hecho== un huerto en la azotea.",
              "en": "This year the neighbors have made a garden on the roof."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
